{"id": "EUVD-2026-108843", "enisaUuid": "634d7098-52bf-3714-99a8-b32f31ec05fd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ngve: fix napi_disable deadlock when attempting to disable XSK pools\n\nWhen disabling XSK pools, GVE calls the unlocked versions of\nnapi_disable and napi_enable. However, the netdev lock has already been\nacquired before ndo_bpf is called because GVE supports queue management\nops. Calling the unlocked versions of napi_disable/enable results in a\ndeadlock when attempting to disable XSK pools, as the thread attempts to\nre-acquire a lock it already holds.\n\nUpdate the NAPI calls to use the locked versions.\n\nThis issue was found in production.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:22:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:22:13", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/42935a61001927aa01db10b53b420efd37eaa99b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d377911ce81fd4e61af814e750d8e08879a5208", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0cb6939a4dfefa822007b7a71986e06bc4f61f54"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99048"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "8ab5f1b7-598d-3297-98cd-ddf7b7c786db", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "606048cbd8346e616cfaee01b0143d072534136d <3d377911ce81fd4e61af814e750d8e08879a5208"}, {"id": "944fbc7a-e69d-35b8-b112-81c6bc80b866", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "a72d8f4c-e8eb-328c-80bb-a6408583d3af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.16"}, {"id": "b10e5209-5495-34f6-b571-6b2a63c841a0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "606048cbd8346e616cfaee01b0143d072534136d <0cb6939a4dfefa822007b7a71986e06bc4f61f54"}, {"id": "c926b1ba-c22c-3149-ad4e-666af57962a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "606048cbd8346e616cfaee01b0